.TITLE "df"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Displays the amount of available disk space. It reports information about __mounted filesystems__ including total size, used space, and capacity.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**df**
Lists all mounted filesystems and their disk space usage in blocks.
> 

**df -h**
Displays disk space usage in human-readable formats like MB, GB, or TB.
> __-h__ human-readable flag

**df -H**
Shows disk space usage using powers of 1000 instead of 1024.
> __-H__ powers of 1000 flag

**df -i**
Reports the number of used and free inodes for each filesystem.
> __-i__ inodes flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
The __-h__ flag is the most common way to view disk space as it provides easily digestible figures. Regularly checking __df__ ensures you do not run out of space on critical partitions.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:du** **mac:mount**

